/*
Expected output:
check
always 1
check
detect boom
always 2
after 2

A check block with both a detect block and an always block, run twice. The
first time nothing goes wrong: the check block runs, the detect block is
skipped and the always block runs. The second time the check block raises an
error: the detect block runs first, then the always block, then the program
carries on after the check block.
*/

class Main
    integer count = 0

    action Main
        Run(false)
        Run(true)
        output "after " + count
    end

    action Run(boolean fail)
        check
            output "check"
            if fail
                alert("boom")
            end
        detect e
            output "detect " + e:GetErrorMessage()
        always
            count = count + 1
            output "always " + count
        end
    end
end
